{# Allow-list anchor ruleset for baseline.pf (FreeBSD). Mirrors
   baseline.firewalld's default-zone semantics: block inbound except the
   declared services, keep loopback open, and trust the NetBird mesh
   interface (wt0 by default). Outbound stays at PF's default (pass).
   Service entries use /etc/services names (ssh, http, ...) or bare
   ports. NOTE: PF is first-match-wins — an earlier broad `pass in all`
   in the host's pf.conf passes traffic before this anchor is reached;
   the anchor cannot override a wider pre-existing pass. #}
block in
pass in quick on lo0
{% for svc in services %}
pass in proto tcp from any to any port {{ svc }}
{% endfor %}
{% if nb_enabled and nb_trusted %}
pass in on {{ nb_iface }}
{% endif %}
